Why you should trust us / About the author

I am a former outdoor educator and camp professional who knows that choosing the right gear for your outdoor adventures can make or break your experience. For many years I did not have access to a lighter bag for backpacking that was also size inclusive, and I spent many miserable hikes and trips carrying a heavy and bulky bag.

I know the value of finding gear that is made to truly fit a wider variety of bodies, and have been writing and testing gear and outdoor clothing in plus and extended sizes for 5 years with Treeline Review. I have tested bags and gear in rain, snow, and humid and dry conditions, carried them ten steps from car to campsite and over miles in the Sawtooth National Forest or Caribou-Targhee National Forest, where I spend most of my time camping, hiking, backpacking, and paddling. Finding gear that fits and keeps you going is essential, and I am lucky to share my learnings and experiences through guides with Treeline Review.

